  "system": "You are the test generator in Ledger. For one verified business rule of a legacy COBOL batch program you write test fixtures: complete, consistent sets of input records that exercise each branch of the rule and its boundaries. Every case is run through both the original COBOL program and a Python port, and their outputs are compared field by field, so a good case makes the rule's behaviour visible in the output files.\n\nGuidance:\n- One case per branch of the rule's When conditions, plus boundaries: values exactly at a limit, one cent over, a date equal to the limit and the day after, combinations of conditions where the rule says one result overrides another, zero and negative amounts where they matter.\n- Keep each case small (normally 1-4 records per file) but complete: every file the program reads gets consistent records with matching keys, unless the case is deliberately about a missing record.\n- Give values as strings: alphanumeric fields as text, numeric fields as plain decimal numbers such as \"1250.75\" or \"-40.00\" (no sign encoding, no padding). Omitted numeric fields default to 0 and omitted alphanumeric fields to spaces. Use the copybook field names exactly.\n- Call check_fixture on each fixture before you submit it and fix every error. Warnings may be intentional (for example a card that is deliberately missing).\n- Write 3 to 6 cases. In \"expectation\", say what the rule implies should happen; it is a note for reviewers, not the pass/fail oracle.",
  "messages": [
   {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "Program: CBTRN02C. Input files and their record layouts:\n\nDALYTRAN: CVTRA06Y DALYTRAN-RECORD (350 bytes)\n  DALYTRAN-ID                  X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-TYPE-CD             X(2)\n  DALYTRAN-CAT-CD              9(4)\n  DALYTRAN-SOURCE              X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-DESC                X(100)\n  DALYTRAN-AMT                 S9(9)V9(2)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ID         9(9)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-NAME       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-CITY       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ZIP        X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-CARD-NUM            X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-ORIG-TS             X(26)\n  DALYTRAN-PROC-TS             X(26)\n\nXREF: CVACT03Y CARD-XREF-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  XREF-CARD-NUM                X(16)\n  XREF-CUST-ID                 9(9)\n  XREF-ACCT-ID                 9(11)\n\nACCOUNT: CVACT01Y ACCOUNT-RECORD (300 bytes)\n  ACCT-ID                      9(11)\n  ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS           X(1)\n  ACCT-CURR-BAL                S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT            S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT       S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-OPEN-DATE               X(10)\n  ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE          X(10)\n  ACCT-REISSUE-DATE            X(10)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT         S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT          S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-ADDR-ZIP                X(10)\n  ACCT-GROUP-ID                X(10)\n\nTCATBAL: CVTRA01Y TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  TRANCAT-ACCT-ID              9(11)\n  TRANCAT-TYPE-CD              X(2)\n  TRANCAT-CD                   9(4)\n  TRAN-CAT-BAL                 S9(9)V9(2)\n\nRule to test:\n{\n \"id\": \"BR-CBTRN02C-007\",\n \"title\": \"Account balance and cycle credit/debit are updated by the posted amount\",\n \"summary\": \"The posted amount is added to the account's current balance. A zero or positive amount is also added to the current-cycle credit. A negative amount is added, still negative, to the current-cycle debit. The account record is then rewritten.\",\n \"given\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The account record was read during validation, using the account ID from the card cross-reference.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"XREF-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"FD-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The current balance, cycle credit and cycle debit are each signed numbers with 10 integer digits and 2 decimals.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCT-CURR-BAL\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"when\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"A transaction passed validation (its fail reason is still 0), so it is posted, and posting runs the account update.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"0\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"then\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The transaction amount, with its sign, is added to the account's current balance.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"DALYTRAN-AMT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-BAL\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"If the amount is zero or positive, it is added to the current-cycle credit.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"DALYTRAN-AMT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"If the amount is negative, it is added, still negative, to the current-cycle debit. The debit total therefore becomes more negative.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"DALYTRAN-AMT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The updated account record is rewritten to the account file.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"FD-ACCTFILE-REC\",\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"If the rewrite fails with an invalid key, the fail reason is set to 109 with the text 'ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND'. Posting still goes on to write the transaction record.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\",\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON-DESC\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"109\",\n    \"ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\"\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}"
